---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/usgaap/asc321.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        {
          id: "s1",
          label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage",
        },
        {
          id: "s2",
          label: "Scope & Applicability",
        },
        {
          id: "s3",
          label: "General Measurement — Fair Value Through Net Income",
        },
        {
          id: "s4",
          label: "Observable Price Change Adjustments Under the Alternative",
        },
        {
          id: "s5",
          label: "Worked Example — Fair Value Change Through Net Income",
        },
        {
          id: "s6",
          label: "Disclosure Requirements",
        },
        {
          id: "s7",
          label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates",
        },
        {
          id: "s8",
          label: "ASC 321 vs IFRS 9 — the FVOCI Election Divergence",
        },
        {
          id: "s9",
          label: "Statement Mapping",
        },
        {
          id: "s10",
          label: "Related Topics",
        },
        {
          id: "s11",
          label: "Glossary",
        },
        {
          id: "history",
          label: "History & Development",
        },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci"><div class="ctitle ci">A deliberate simplification favouring a single measurement basis</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">Before ASU 2016-01, equity securities classified as AFS were measured at fair value with changes in OCI — the FASB concluded this produced information LESS useful than routing all equity fair value changes directly through NET INCOME, on the basis that equity investment performance is a genuine part of an entity's current-period economic results, not a deferred item. ASC 321 reflects that conclusion: essentially ALL equity securities with a readily determinable fair value now flow through net income, full stop.</div></div>
      <div class="card cs"><div class="ctitle cs">The Topic that most starkly separates from IFRS 9</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 321 is the primary SOURCE of the single most consequential OCI-related divergence between US GAAP and IFRS covered elsewhere in this library (in the ASC 220 poster) — IFRS 9's equity FVOCI election has NO US GAAP counterpart at all, making this Topic worth understanding in its own right as the origin of that difference.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope &amp; Applicability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Equity securities with limited exceptions</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 321 applies to investments in EQUITY SECURITIES — instruments representing an ownership interest in an entity, such as common and preferred stock — EXCEPT for investments accounted for under the EQUITY METHOD (ASC 323, where the investor has significant influence) or CONSOLIDATED subsidiaries (where the investor has control), both of which fall outside ASC 321's scope and are addressed by their own dedicated Topics instead.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>General Measurement — Fair Value Through Net Income</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">The default (and essentially only) rule</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Equity securities with a READILY DETERMINABLE fair value (e.g. actively traded on an exchange) are measured at FAIR VALUE, with ALL changes in fair value — both unrealised holding gains/losses during the period AND realised gains/losses on sale — recognised in NET INCOME. There is NO OCI classification election available, unlike debt securities under ASC 320's AFS category.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Observable Price Change Adjustments Under the Alternative</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Triggered by a specific, identifiable transaction</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">If the entity identifies an OBSERVABLE transaction for the same or a similar security of the same issuer (e.g. a new funding round for a private company at a different implied valuation), the carrying amount under the measurement alternative is ADJUSTED to reflect that observable price, with the resulting adjustment recognised in NET INCOME — consistent with the general "through net income" philosophy applied throughout ASC 321.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Worked Example — Fair Value Change Through Net Income</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A publicly traded equity investment</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Marketable equity securities remeasured at year end</div><div class="wk-body">An entity holds publicly traded shares purchased for $2,000,000. At year end, the fair value of the holding is $2,300,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The $300,000 unrealised gain is recognised ENTIRELY in NET INCOME for the period: Debit Equity investment $300,000 / Credit Unrealised gain on equity securities (net income) $300,000 — NO portion goes through OCI, regardless of the entity's investment intent or holding period.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASC 321 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Carrying amounts of equity securities by measurement approach (fair value vs measurement alternative)</span><span>Amount of unrealised gains/losses recognised in net income during the period, for securities still held at the reporting date</span><span>Impairment losses recognised, and the qualitative factors considered</span><span>Cumulative upward/downward adjustments recognised under the measurement alternative, since inception</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a security has a "readily determinable" fair value, determining whether the measurement alternative is even available</span><span>Whether a transaction is genuinely "similar" enough for the observable price change mechanic to apply</span><span>Qualitative impairment indicator assessment under the measurement alternative</span></div></div>
      <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of an impaired security under the measurement alternative, once an indicator is identified</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>ASC 321 vs IFRS 9 — the FVOCI Election Divergence</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASC 321 vs IFRS 9's equity instrument treatment</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">US GAAP (ASC 321)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 9</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Default measurement</span><span>Fair value through NET INCOME, mandatory</span><span>Fair value through profit or loss (FVTPL), the default</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>OCI election available?</span><span>NEVER — no such election exists</span><span>YES — an IRREVOCABLE election for equity instruments not held for trading, deferring gains/losses in OCI</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Recycling on disposal, if FVOCI elected</span><span>Not applicable</span><span>NEVER recycled to profit or loss, even on sale — a genuinely "permanent OCI" outcome under IFRS 9</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Non-marketable equity practical expedient</span><span>The measurement alternative (cost + observable price changes)</span><span>No directly equivalent named alternative — IFRS 9 still generally requires fair value estimation even for unquoted equity, though with practical guidance on when cost may approximate fair value</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout warn" style="margin-bottom:0;">⚠️ This remains one of the most consequential earnings-volatility differences between the two frameworks — a US GAAP preparer holding a long-term strategic equity stake will see 100% of its fair value swings hit net income every period, while an IFRS preparer holding an economically identical stake CAN elect to shield those swings from profit or loss entirely, via the FVOCI election with no recycling.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every ASC 321 event lands</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Fair value change (readily determinable FV)</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Always net income; never OCI</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Observable price change adjustment (measurement alternative)</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Also always net income</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Impairment under the measurement alternative</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised once qualitative indicators trigger a fair value estimate</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Related Topics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Topic</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 320</span><span>Governs debt securities, split from this Topic's scope since ASU 2016-01</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 323</span><span>Equity Method and Joint Ventures — applies instead where the investor has significant influence, outside ASC 321's scope</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 220</span><span>Confirms this Topic's fair value changes never route through OCI, unlike other comprehensive income components elsewhere</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 820</span><span>Fair Value Measurement — supplies the general fair value framework, and guidance on "readily determinable" fair value</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn"><div class="ctitle cn">Quick-reference glossary preview</div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Readily determinable fair value</div><div class="glossary-def">A fair value that can be reliably established, typically from an active market quote — the threshold determining whether an equity security uses the fair value model or the measurement alternative.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Measurement alternative</div><div class="glossary-def">A practical expedient measuring non-marketable equity securities at cost, adjusted for impairment and observable price changes, rather than requiring a full fair value estimate.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Observable price change</div><div class="glossary-def">A transaction price for an identical or similar security of the same issuer, used to adjust the carrying amount of an equity investment measured under the measurement alternative.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Equity security</div><div class="glossary-def">An instrument representing an ownership interest in an entity, such as common or preferred stock, distinct from a debt security representing a creditor relationship.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.ASC321 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>

